.. raw:: html

    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="Kapustinskii (1956) replaced the structure-specific Madelung constant with a near-universal constant per ion, so KapustinskiiLatticeEnergy needs only the number of ions per formula unit, the charges, and the ionic radii. On rock-salt halides it tracks the structure-based Born-Lande value; it also handles salts of other structures (fluorite CaF2) where no Madelung constant is supplied at all.">

.. only:: html

  .. image:: /api/gallery/crystal/lattice_energy/images/thumb/sphx_glr_plot_02_kapustinskii_thumb.png
    :alt:

  :doc:`/api/gallery/crystal/lattice_energy/plot_02_kapustinskii`

.. raw:: html

      <div class="sphx-glr-thumbnail-title">Kapustinskii equation: lattice energy without a crystal structure</div>
    </div>


.. only:: not html

 * :doc:`/api/gallery/crystal/lattice_energy/plot_02_kapustinskii`

.. raw:: html

    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="Shannon (1976) fitted one self-consistent radius per ion (for a given coordination number) so that cation-anion distances in thousands of crystals are reproduced by simple sums r_++r_-. SHANNON_IONIC_RADII_PM holds the 6-coordinate values; here their sums are checked against measured rock-salt nearest-neighbor distances, and their periodic trends are plotted.">

.. only:: html

  .. image:: /api/gallery/crystal/lattice_energy/images/thumb/sphx_glr_plot_03_shannon_ionic_radii_thumb.png
